    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000011",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Activation is shown in reaction profile diagrams",
    "reading_order" : 11,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000012",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Exothermic reactions",
    "reading_order" : 12,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000013",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "A reaction is exothermic when the products have less energy than the reactants",
    "reading_order" : 13,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000014",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Heat energy is **given off **by the reaction **to the** **surroundings**",
    "reading_order" : 14,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000015",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The **temperature** of the **environment increases** - this can be measured with a thermometer",
    "reading_order" : 15,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000016",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The **energy **of the **system decreases**",
    "reading_order" : 16,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000017",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "There is an enthalpy decrease during the reaction so Δ*H *is negative",
    "reading_order" : 17,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000018",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Exothermic reactions are **thermodynamically **possible (because the enthalpy of the reactants is **higher** than that of the products)",
    "reading_order" : 18,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000019",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "However, if the rate is too slow, the reaction may not occur",
    "reading_order" : 19,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000020",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "In this case the reaction is **kinetically **controlled",
    "reading_order" : 20,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000022",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "***The enthalpy change during an exothermic reaction***",
    "reading_order" : 22,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000023",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Endothermic reactions",
    "reading_order" : 23,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000024",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "A reaction is endothermic when the products have more energy than the reactants",
    "reading_order" : 24,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000025",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Heat energy is **absorbed** **by **the reaction **from **the **surroundings**",
    "reading_order" : 25,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000026",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The **temperature** of the **environment decreases** - this can be measured with a thermometer",
    "reading_order" : 26,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000027",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The **energy **of the **system increases**",
    "reading_order" : 27,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000028",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "There is an enthalpy increase during the reaction so Δ*H *is positive",
